{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmGu89r4sd6E2XhuKbmS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan phase is finished. The brief is in `journal/2026-10-06/20-brief.md`, and `state.json` now has `pack`, `slug`, `title` and, last, `plan: \"done\"`.\n\n**What gets built:** `@one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1`, titled \"Weekly 5k Run Report\". It is a still image for a weekly parkrun-style event summary, hinted at 1080x1080. It must also work at 1920x1080, 1080x1920 and the seven canvases the build checks, down to 480x270.\n\n- **Layout:**\n  - A header with the event name, run number and date.\n  - Two big, equal tiles: finishers and volunteers.\n  - Four smaller tiles: new PBs, first timers, visitors, first-time volunteers. They sit in one row on a square canvas and a 2x2 grid on portrait.\n  - Wide canvases put the two big tiles in a left column and the four small ones in a 2x2 grid on the right.\n  - Under the tiles is a milestone band, then an optional footer line.\n- **Props (8):** `eventName`, `runNumber`, `date`, `counts` (a JSON object with exactly six keys), `milestones`, `footer`, `accent`, `debugLayout`. `milestones` is a text line like `4xR25, 3xR50, 1xR100, 2xV25`, the same format the volunteer stats tool parkrun-runstats prints, plus `V` for volunteer clubs.\n- **Main rulings:**\n  - The card prints only the numbers the user types. It never fetches them and never derives stats from them.\n  - The milestone band stays even in a week with no milestones and shows \"No milestone clubs this week\".\n  - The word \"parkrun\", its logo and its colours appear nowhere in the defaults or the fixed labels.\n  - Every bad input is refused with a message that names the field and the value.\n- **Variants:** (a) the baseline above; (b) all six counts as equal tiles, no big pair; (c) a dark page.\n\n**Weak spots, as written in the brief:**\n- The demand evidence is one Chrome extension's README and two text-only tools.\n- Nobody saw an actual PowerPoint original from the events the scout named.\n- Typing `counts` as JSON is a chore for a volunteer in a hurry.\n- The `V` prefix for volunteer clubs is my own addition; runstats only prints run milestones.\n- At 480x270 the small labels will be about 7-8 px.\n\n**How this call went:** plan call 1 ran out of time while its research agents were still working in the background, and the runner killed them. I recovered the three summaries that had finished from that run's log, and saved them to `journal/2026-10-06/plan-notes/` for the build phase. Because this was the last plan call and only had 15 minutes, I wrote the brief myself rather than starting new background work. The fourth summary, on parkrun itself, never finished, so those facts come from the scout's notes. No independent agent reviewed the brief before I marked it done.\n\nI also recorded `model.selfDeclared: \"claude-opus-5.5\"` in `run.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":866,"cache_read_input_tokens":92381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":866},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78d8a59d-21d2-4a02-b677-90d698336c75","uuid":"3249ac1b-5135-4f0c-8d20-c3f7ab542eb1","timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:10:13.713Z","request_id":"req_011CfmGu7rVtnRmx9SQxo8Vw"}
